# MediTrack Project Rules

## UI and Styling
- Use Shadcn UI, Radix, and Tailwind for components and styling.
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind CSS; use a mobile-first approach.

## Page Patterns

### Card Selection Pages (tipo select-type)
When creating new pages with card selection patterns, follow these standards:

**Layout Structure:**
- Use AppSidebarLayout for consistent navigation
- Include back button (ArrowLeft icon) positioned top-left with Button variant="ghost" size="icon"
- Page title as h1 with text-2xl font-bold
- Subtitle/description with text-muted-foreground class

**Card Design:**
- Cards should be square with consistent spacing
- Use grid layout: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6`
- Card classes: `cursor-pointer transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg hover:scale-105 border-2 hover:border-primary/50`

**Card Content:**
- Centered icon in rounded container with `mx-auto mb-4 p-3 bg-primary/10 rounded-full w-fit`
- Icon size: `h-8 w-8 text-primary`
- CardTitle with `text-lg`
- CardDescription with `text-sm leading-relaxed`
- Action button at bottom with full width: `w-full` size="sm"
- Plus icon in button: `<Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />`

**Example Structure:**
```tsx
<Card className="cursor-pointer transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg hover:scale-105 border-2 hover:border-primary/50">
  <CardHeader className="text-center pb-4">
    <div className="mx-auto mb-4 p-3 bg-primary/10 rounded-full w-fit">
      <IconComponent className="h-8 w-8 text-primary" />
    </div>
    <CardTitle className="text-lg">{title}</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="text-center">
    <CardDescription className="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      {description}
    </CardDescription>
    <div className="mt-4">
      <Button className="w-full" size="sm">
        <Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
        {actionText}
      </Button>
    </div>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Form Pages (tipo create-by-type)
When creating form pages, follow these standards:

**Layout Structure:**
- Use AppLayout for main container
- Container with: `container mx-auto p-6 space-y-6 max-w-none`
- Header section with back button, title, and description
- Form with: `space-y-6 w-full max-w-6xl mx-auto`

**Header Pattern:**
```tsx
<div className="flex items-center gap-4">
  <Link href={backRoute}>
    <Button variant="ghost" size="icon">
      <ArrowLeft className="h-4 w-4" />
    </Button>
  </Link>
  <div>
    <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold">{pageTitle}</h1>
    <p className="text-muted-foreground">
      {pageDescription}
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Form Sections:**
- Organize form fields in separate Card components for logical grouping
- Each Card should have CardHeader with CardTitle and CardDescription
- Use CardContent for form fields with `space-y-4` class
- Grid layouts for related fields: `grid grid-cols-2 gap-4` or `grid grid-cols-3 gap-4`

**Form Section Structure:**
```tsx
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Section Title</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription>
      Section description explaining the purpose
    </CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="space-y-4">
    {/* Form fields with proper spacing and validation */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

**Action Buttons:**
- Place at the end of the form
- Use: `flex justify-end gap-4`
- Cancel button: `Button type="button" variant="outline"`
- Submit button: `Button type="submit" disabled={processing}`
- Show loading state in submit button text

**Form Validation:**
- Include comprehensive validation for all required fields
- Display error messages below each field with: `text-sm text-destructive`
- Use appropriate input types and constraints
- Include confirmation dialogs or alerts for important actions

**Field Guidelines:**
- Use proper Label components with htmlFor attributes
- Mark required fields with asterisk (*)
- Use appropriate input types (email, tel, number, date, etc.)
- Include helpful placeholders
- Group related fields logically

## Code Quality Rules

### Bug Fixes:
- Analyze the problem thoroughly before suggesting fixes
- Provide precise, targeted solutions
- Explain the root cause of the bug

### Keep It Simple:
- Prioritize readability and maintainability
- Avoid over-engineering solutions
- Use standard libraries and patterns when possible

### Code Changes:
- Propose a clear plan before making changes
- Apply all modifications to a single file at once
- Do not alter unrelated files
